an7.36:2.1 starts: “He gives what is beautiful,
an7.36:2.2 starts: hard to give;
an7.36:2.3 starts: does what is hard to do;
an7.36:2.4 starts: endures painful, ill-spoken words.
an7.36:4.1 starts: A person in whom
an7.36:4.2 starts: these traits are found,
an7.36:4.3 starts: is a friend to be cultivated
an7.36:4.4 starts: by anyone wanting a friend.”
an7.64:22.1 starts: Doing these deeds
an7.64:22.2 starts: that kill beings
# superseded: an7.64:22.3 starts: and do violence to himself,
# superseded: an7.64:22.4 starts: the angry person doesn’t realize he’s ruined.
an8.30:23.1 starts: Knowing my thoughts,
an8.30:23.2 starts: the Teacher, unexcelled in the cosmos,
an8.30:23.3 starts: came to me through his power
an8.30:23.4 starts: in a body made of mind.
an8.54:15.1 starts: “Heedful at administering
an8.54:15.2 starts: or working at one’s occupation,
an8.54:15.3 starts: maintaining one’s life in tune,
an8.54:15.4 starts: one protects one’s store of wealth.
an7.64:20.1 starts: Like oneself, all beings
an7.64:20.2 starts: hold themselves most dear,
an7.64:20.3 starts: yet an angry person, deranged,
an7.64:20.4 starts: can kill himself in many ways:
an8.54:17.1 starts: Thus for one who seeks the household life,
an8.54:17.2 starts: these eight qualities—
# superseded: an8.54:17.3 none
# superseded: an8.54:17.4 starts: leading to welfare & happiness
# superseded: an8.54:18.1 starts: both in this life & in lives to
# superseded: an8.54:18.2 starts: have been declared by the one
an8.54:18.3 starts: And this is how, for householders,
an8.54:18.4 starts: generosity & merit increase.”
an10.118:4.1 starts: But those who practice Dhamma
an10.118:4.2 starts: in line with the well-taught Dhamma,
an10.118:4.3 starts: will cross over
an10.118:4.4 starts: the realm of Death
an10.118:7.1 starts: Whose minds are well-developed
an10.118:7.2 starts: in the factors for self-awakening,
an10.118:7.3 starts: who delight in non-clinging,
an10.118:7.4 starts: relinquishing grasping—
an10.118:7.5 starts: resplendent,
an10.118:7.6 starts: They, in the world,
dhp1:1 starts: Phenomena are
dhp1:2 starts: ruled by the heart,
dhp1:3 starts: If you speak or act
dhp1:4 starts: with a corrupted heart,
dhp1:5 starts: then suffering follows you –
dhp1:6 starts: as the wheel of the cart,
dhp2:1 starts: Phenomena are
dhp2:2 starts: ruled by the heart,
dhp2:3 starts: If you speak or act
dhp2:4 starts: with a calm, bright heart,
dhp2:5 starts: then happiness follows you,
dhp2:6 starts: like a shadow
